---
description: Homelab service icons — source app icons from selfh.st and keep assets under public/
globs: lib/homelabCatalogIcons.ts,lib/homelabCatalogIcons.generated.ts,scripts/sync-homelab-icons.mjs,public/assets/selfh-icons/*
alwaysApply: false
---

Homelab cards and the architecture graph read the Backstage v2 catalog only (`/api/site/catalog/v2`); the icon is keyed by entity name (`lib/homelabCatalogIcons.ts`). When adding or updating a service icon:

1. **Find icons first** on [selfh.st/icons](https://selfh.st/icons/) and match the app name to the CDN slug used by [selfhst/icons](https://github.com/selfhst/icons) (PNG path pattern: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/selfhst/icons@main/png/<slug>.png`).
2. **Vendor into the repo** under `public/assets/selfh-icons/` (kebab-case filename, e.g. `portainer.png`); never hotlink a third-party CDN for card icons.
3. Map the entity name to the file in `nabla-compose/catalog/service-icons.json` (`webAssets`), then regenerate `lib/homelabCatalogIcons.generated.ts` with `node scripts/sync-homelab-icons.mjs --source ../nabla-compose/catalog/service-icons.json`. Never edit the generated file by hand.
4. An unknown entity falls back to its parent's icon, then to `generic-app.svg`; upstream image URLs are ignored.
5. When editing copy around the homelab grids, include a reader link to [selfh.st/apps](https://selfh.st/apps/) for discovering more FOSS / self-hosted applications.
